[h1]Can't connect from a phone or tablet?[/h1]

[i]In other languages:[/i] [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/german/phone-connection-troubleshooting.md]Deutsch[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/spanish/phone-connection-troubleshooting.md]Español (España)[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/latam/phone-connection-troubleshooting.md]Español (Latinoamérica)[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/french/phone-connection-troubleshooting.md]Français[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/italian/phone-connection-troubleshooting.md]Italiano[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/polish/phone-connection-troubleshooting.md]Polski[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/brazilian/phone-connection-troubleshooting.md]Português (Brasil)[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/turkish/phone-connection-troubleshooting.md]Türkçe[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/russian/phone-connection-troubleshooting.md]Русский[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/thai/phone-connection-troubleshooting.md]ไทย[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/japanese/phone-connection-troubleshooting.md]日本語[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/schinese/phone-connection-troubleshooting.md]简体中文[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/koreana/phone-connection-troubleshooting.md]한국어[/url]

Try these steps if your phone or tablet cannot connect. For crashes or problems during a run, see [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/discussion/3799476240/563668239243120957/]Having a problem? Post it here[/url].

[h3]1. Choose the connection settings[/h3]

On the computer running the game, open [b]Couch Co-Op QR Code[/b].

[list]
[*][b]Network interface[/b] (left): choose [b]Wired (Ethernet)[/b] if the computer connects to your router by cable, or [b]Wi-Fi[/b] if it connects wirelessly. Choose the connection to the router your phone uses. Skip [b]PC name (.local)[/b].
[*][b]Connection method[/b] (right): choose [b]Direct address[/b], without “(HTTPS)”. The address should start with [i]http://[/i], for example [i]http://192.168.1.5:13337[/i].
[/list]

Scan the QR code again after changing these settings.

Use [b]Direct address[/b] while troubleshooting. The HTTPS methods are optional choices for performance and security, with extra setup or connection requirements.

[h3]2. Check the phone’s network[/h3]

[list]
[*]Connect the phone to your home Wi-Fi, not the [b]Guest[/b] network. The computer can use either Wi-Fi or a cable to the same router.
[*]Make sure the phone is using Wi-Fi rather than mobile data.
[*]Temporarily disconnect any VPN on the phone or computer. Phone ad blockers that use a VPN connection count too.
[/list]

[b]If the page opens but gets stuck joining, skip to step 6.[/b]

[h3]3. Windows: allow the game through the firewall[/h3]

On your home network:

[olist]
[*]Open [b]Settings > Network & Internet > Wi-Fi[/b] (or [b]Ethernet[/b]), select your network, and set [b]Network profile type[/b] to [b]Private[/b].
[*]Open [b]Windows Security > Firewall & network protection > Allow an app through firewall[/b].
[*]Find [b]Slay the Spire 2[/b] and tick [b]Private[/b]. If it is missing, choose [b]Allow another app...[/b] and select the game’s [i].exe[/i] file.
[/olist]

If you previously cancelled the game’s firewall prompt, remove its blocked entry and add the game again.

If your antivirus has its own firewall, allow the game there too.

Opening the address on the computer running the game does not test whether the firewall allows your phone to connect.

[h3]4. Check whether the browser is forcing HTTPS[/h3]

The [b]Direct address[/b] method uses [i]http://[/i]. If your browser tries to change it to [i]https://[/i], check its secure-connection setting:

[list]
[*]Chrome: [b]Settings > Privacy and security > Security > Always use secure connections[/b]
[*]Firefox: [b]Settings > Privacy and security > Connection and software security > Advanced settings > HTTPS-Only Mode[/b]
[/list]

Allow the HTTP address, then scan the QR code again. Keep [b]Direct address[/b] selected on the computer.

[h3]5. Check the router[/h3]

Guest Wi-Fi often prevents devices from connecting to each other. Use the main home network.

If both devices are already on that network, check whether your router has [b]AP isolation[/b], [b]Client isolation[/b], or [b]Wireless isolation[/b] enabled. These settings block devices from reaching each other.

If you use a Wi-Fi extender, check that it is in [b]access point[/b] or [b]bridge[/b] mode rather than creating a separate network.

[h3]6. If the page opens but joining takes a while[/h3]

Starting a player’s game can take up to a minute. Keep the page open while the progress line under [b]Joining…[/b] changes stage.

If an error appears, take a screenshot or copy its exact wording, including any smaller grey line.

If it stays on [b]Joining…[/b] or [b]Loading…[/b] without an error, include the last progress message when you post below.

[h3]7. If it worked before[/h3]

The computer’s address may have changed after reconnecting to the network or restarting the router. Open the QR screen and scan again.

If an old bookmark or home-screen shortcut no longer works, replace it using the newly scanned address.

[hr][/hr]

[h1]Still stuck? Post here[/h1]

Start with:

[list]
[*]How far it gets: no page, no player list, stuck joining/loading, or disconnected during play.
[*]A screenshot or the exact error message.
[*]The computer’s operating system, plus the phone model and browser.
[*]Whether every phone fails or just one.
[/list]

[h3]Copy the connection report[/h3]

On the computer, open [b]Couch Co-Op QR Code[/b], then look under [b]Connections[/b]. Select the failed connection under [b]Connection problems[/b], choose [b]Copy report[/b], and paste it into your post.

If no connection appears there, say so and post the details above.

The report includes the paths to the relevant log files. If logs are needed, [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/discussion/3799476240/563668239243120957/]Having a problem? Post it here[/url] explains how to find them. Before posting logs publicly, remove your Steam account ID and computer user name if you prefer to keep them private.

Use the mod on a network you trust: anyone who can reach the join address can open the client and play.
